# /sdd-intents

Purpose:
  Classify, track, and route user intents through the SDDRA chain graph.
  Bridges the gap between raw prompts in prompts/inbox/ and executable
  chain arms (P1, D1, S1, C1, R1, DEP1).

Owns: commands/sdd-intents.sdd

Description:
  Reads prompts/inbox/, prompts/active/, and .sdd/intents/INDEX.sdd
  to produce an intent pipeline report. Classifies each pending prompt
  by likely chain arm based on keyword matching and intent signals.
  Shows pipeline status, blockers, completion rate, and routing
  recommendations.

Usage:
  /sdd-intents
  /sdd-intents --pipeline
  /sdd-intents --classify
  /sdd-intents --blockers
  /sdd-intents --json

Options:
  --pipeline   Show full intent pipeline with chain arm assignments
  --classify   Re-classify all pending prompts
  --blockers   Show only intents blocked by dependencies or approvals
  --json       Output machine-readable JSON

Mode: READ_ONLY (--classify is READ_WRITE)

ChainArmMapping:
  keywords:
    "write / plan / design / document" -> D1 (Documentation)
    "implement / code / build / develop" -> C1 (Code Generation)
    "review / audit / test / verify" -> R1 (Review)
    "deploy / release / publish" -> DEP1 (Deploy)
    "analyze / explain / understand" -> P1 (Prompt Analysis)
    "spec / define / model / schema" -> S1 (SDD Generation)

Output:
  INTENT PIPELINE

    Pending:       <count>
    Classified:    <count>
    Unclassified:  <count>
    Blocked:       <count>
    Completion:    <percentage>%

  Intent List:
    [INT-001] arm: C1 | priority: high | prompt: "Implement refund service"
    [INT-002] arm: R1 | priority: medium | prompt: "Review payment module"
    [INT-003] arm: UNKNOWN | priority: low | prompt: "Fix typo in README"
    [INT-004] arm: C1 | priority: high | blocked: waiting on DEC-102

Rules:
  [INT-01] /sdd-intents MUST NOT modify any file unless --classify is supplied.
  [INT-02] Intent classification MUST use keyword matching as primary signal.
  [INT-03] Unclassified intents MUST be surfaced for human review.
  [INT-04] Blocked intents MUST identify the blocking dependency or approval.
  [INT-05] Completion rate MUST be calculated as classified / total pending.
  [INT-06] --classify mode MUST require human approval before updating intent tags.

Navigation:
   INDEX: @INDEX.sdd
   Intents: @../intents/INDEX.sdd
   ChainGraph: @../chains/graph.sdd
   PromptsInbox: @../../prompts/inbox/
   PromptsActive: @../../prompts/active/
   Projects: @../projects/INDEX.sdd

State: +
